---
import InsertLayout from '../../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/jsonld';
import '../../styles/proofs.css';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Working samples', url: '/proofs/' }
]);
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Working samples"
  description="Run two bounded Toledo software demonstrations: exact-byte request signing with safe retry states, and a searchable purchasing archive. Synthetic data, source and test results included."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="Working samples."
  subheading="Run the evidence. Read the limits."
>
  <p>
    These two demonstrations make a specific behavior inspectable. Each includes
    source, repeatable checks, and a record of what remains untested. Both use
    invented data. Neither is a client deployment.
  </p>

  <section class="proof-sample" aria-labelledby="signing-heading">
    <div class="proof-kicker">01 / Request signing and order safety</div>
    <h2 id="signing-heading">Keep the bytes fixed. Make retries deliberate.</h2>
    <p>
      A request signature breaks when the transmitted body differs from the
      signed body. A second recharge can happen when a lost response is treated
      as permission to try again. This offline proof checks both boundaries.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>39 local tests passed.</strong> OpenSSL independently verified a generated
      RSA signature. The order simulation suppresses duplicate events and holds uncertain
      outcomes for reconciliation.
    </p>
    <div class="proof-links">
      <a href="/proofs/request-signing/">Inspect the request-signing proof →</a>
      <a
        href="/proofs/request-signing/request-signing-proof.zip"
        download
        data-astro-reload>Download signing source and tests (ZIP)</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-sample" aria-labelledby="archive-heading">
    <div class="proof-kicker">02 / An owned purchasing archive</div>
    <h2 id="archive-heading">
      Find an old purchase. Keep its source attached.
    </h2>
    <p>
      A supplied CSV becomes a searchable purchasing book with original record
      references. Currency totals stay separate. Missing received quantities
      stay unknown. Rejected and duplicate records remain accounted for.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>22 local tests passed.</strong> The invented fixture contains three
      purchase orders and two suppliers. It demonstrates the processing core; compatibility
      with an actual Stocky export is unverified.
    </p>
    <div class="proof-links">
      <a href="/proofs/purchasing/">Inspect the purchasing-archive proof →</a>
      <a href="/proofs/purchasing/archive.html" data-astro-reload
        >Open the working archive</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Who did the work</h2>
  <p>
    AI agents built and checked these samples for Toledo Technologies LLC. Human
    review is not represented as part of this evidence. For an AI-operated
    engagement, Toledo remains the supplier; the written scope identifies the
    delivery model, access, acceptance checks, and limits.
  </p>
  <p>
    A real integration starts with its own code, provider documentation, and
    authorized test environment. A passing sample does not establish that a
    merchant's system has been repaired.
  </p>
  <div class="proof-links">
    <a href="/about/">Read how the practice operates →</a>
    <a href="/portfolio/">Read the separate research and portfolio ledger →</a>
  </div>
</InsertLayout>
